.</span> </span>). </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"4\"><span class=\"lex-n\">b</span> <span class=\"gk\">θατέρᾳ</span> (sc. <span class=\"gk\">ἡμέρᾳ</span>) <b class=\"lex-tr\">on the morrow</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">782</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Rh.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">449</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τῆς ἑτέρας</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Cri.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">44a</span> </span>; but <span class=\"gk\">τῇ ἑτέρᾳ</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">on the following</b> (i.e. <b class=\"lex-tr\">the third) day</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Cyr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">4.6.10</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"4\"><span class=\"lex-n\">c</span> (sc. <span class=\"gk\">ὁδῷ</span>) <b class=\"lex-tr\">in another</b> or <b class=\"lex-tr\">a different way</b>, <span class=\"gk\">καὶ τῇδε φῦναι χἀτέρᾳ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OC</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1444</span> </span>; <b class=\"lex-tr\">another way</b>, <span class=\"gk\">τρέπεσθαι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Nu.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">812</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἑτέρᾳ πῃ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Eq.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">35</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τότ' ἄλλος'.., θατέρᾳ δὲ</span>.. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Tr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">272</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">θατέρᾳ.., θατέρᾳ</span>.. <b class=\"lex-tr\">in one way.., in the other</b>.., <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Henioch.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.16</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἑτέρηφι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hes.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Op.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">216</span> </span>: acc. <span class=\"gk\">ἑτέραν ἐκτρέπεσθαι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Luc.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Tim.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">2</span> adverb. with Preps.: </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"4\"><span class=\"lex-n\">a</span> <span class=\"gk\">ἐπὶ θάτερα</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">to the one</b> or <b class=\"lex-tr\">the other side, one</b> or <b class=\"lex-tr\">the other way</b>, <span class=\"gk\">ἐπὶ μὲν θάτερα.., ἐπὶ θ. δὲ</span>.. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hp.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Art.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τότε μὲν ἐπὶ θάτερα, τότε δ' ἐπὶ θ</span>. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Sph.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">259c</span> </span>: also with another Prep., <span class=\"gk\">ἐς τὰ ἐπὶ θάτερα</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">to</b> or <b class=\"lex-tr\">on the other side</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Th.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.87</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἐκ τοῦ ἐπὶ θάτερα</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">from the other side</b>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">7.37</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἐκ μὲν τοῦ ἐπὶ θ., ἐ